    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI think a video would be better. In the video, I wish to comment and uncomment a block, but I can't uncomment it.\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/31820255/229094109-c6335647-97c0-44aa-93d7-090a64723602.mp4\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSet `ignore_blank_lines = true` in lua config for `mini.comment`.\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nBasically, with `ignore_blank_lines` option set to true, I would expect empty lines to be ignored during the uncommenting part as well.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`mini.comment` is not able uncomment blocks if a blank line is there inside the block.",
